    "title": "Who the subgraph calls the API as",
    "status": "resolved",
    "date": "2026-10-21",
    "phase": "select",
    "question": "Every request carries one service bearer token, so any client the supergraph lets through can read any customer's orders, IBANs (D-a39c6a) and integration webhook URLs, and can create, update and cancel orders. Forward the caller's own token so the API enforces per-user access, or keep the service token and have the router require authentication on those fields? (@authenticated/@requiresScopes are licensed router features this target leaves out of the workspace schema: federation-subgraph.md; they would be a change in your own graph.)",
